{ fp_registers_busy.init - a DSEE derived object of be_com/opcodes.def
  (cc.a88k only): the floating registers each opcode reads and writes,
  counted in singles (a double 2), as two bytes by opcode: reads at
  2 opc, writes at 2 opc + 1.  Included by sched.pas (after
  exs.ins.pas, before utils.ins.pas), whose instr_would_fit keeps a
  cycle's floating register reads and writes within sched_3158 (set by
  lir_main) and whose fit_instr adds an issued instruction's to the
  cycle's counts.

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from the DOMAIN C 6.9 binary
  cc.a88k, the section sched_readonly_tables (0x2BE108, 768 bytes: the
  opcodes 0..383, those past opc$adj_move (211) all zero).  The
  section's name is the unit's (as lir_main_readonly_tables and
  zzzzz_readonly_tables): a variable of sched's own, laid out in a
  section of the module's name.

  Not known from the original: the variable's name (the derived
  object's), its type and the file's layout. }

var (sched_readonly_tables)
